  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Xyrem / Xywav oxybate CNS depressants, Version 2; effective 2021-01-11. Single xyrem pack covers sodium_oxybate (Xyrem) and calcium, magnesium, potassium and sodium oxybates (Xywav).",
    "Approval criteria 1-9 and explicit denial criteria encoded. Both closed narcolepsy indications share approval gates. Heart failure, uncontrolled hypertension and impaired renal function denials apply only to Xyrem. Diagnosis letter, REMS enrollment, drug screen, evaluations, therapy failures and sleep logs are attestations requiring manual review.",
    "Approval criterion 8 repeats contraindication to stimulant use; encoded as contraindication to the wakefulness-promoting therapy step, consistent with the requested interpretation.",
    "Cautions (notes only): depression and suicidality; impaired motor and cognitive function; high sodium content of Xyrem; evaluate for sleepwalking.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 6 months if responding positively and dose does not exceed 9 g/day. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 3 × 180ml bottles; maximum 9 g/day. Source prints 9 mg/day in reauthorization and quantity sections; retained here as 9 g/day per task specification, with the source discrepancy flagged for manual review. No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "PDL status unknown. Documentation verification, cautions, duration, reauthorization, dose and quantity remain manual review."
  ],
